{"name":"Oyster Bar","hex":"#dbd0bb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"oyster bar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A restaurant, or part of a restaurant, that specializes in serving oysters, often buffet-style."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oyster_bar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Oyster bar","blocks":[{"text":"An oyster bar, also known as an oyster saloon, oyster house or a raw bar service, is a restaurant specializing in serving oysters, or a section of a restaurant which serves oysters buffet-style. Oysters have been consumed since ancient times and were common tavern food in Europe, but the oyster bar as a distinct restaurant began making an appearance in the 18th century."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Arnauds.jpg/330px-Arnauds.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oyster_bar","wikidata":"Q7116364"},{"title":"Oyster","blocks":[{"text":"Oyster is the common name for a number of different families of salt-water bivalve molluscs that live in marine or brackish habitats. In some species, the valves are highly calcified, and many are somewhat irregular in shape. Many oysters are in the superfamily Ostreoidea."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Crassostrea_gigas_p1040848.jpg/330px-Crassostrea_gigas_p1040848.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oyster","wikidata":"Q107411"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Harriet_Mawhinney%26husband_Samuel.jpg/500px-Harriet_Mawhinney%26husband_Samuel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Harriet_Mawhinney%26husband_Samuel.jpg/500px-Harriet_Mawhinney%26husband_Samuel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_co